###########################################################################
# OBO Foundry class alignments
###########################################################################
#
# The rationale below is kept even where the axiom is now a comment: it is why
# the mapping is what it is, and it is not recorded anywhere else. Each axiom is
# asserted once, in the module that defines the class, following the convention
# this file already used for sstim:SessionInstance -> prov:Activity.

# Sensory stimulation intervention → planned process.
# OBI_0000011 is obsolete and must not appear in live logical axioms. SSTIM
# uses the active, broader COB_0000082 'planned process' term because an
# intervention need not be completely executed (verified via OLS, 2026-07-10).
# sstim:SensoryStimulationIntervention rdfs:subClassOf cob:0000082 .
#   Asserted in sstim-session.ttl; commented here so the Full closure does
#   not carry the axiom twice.

# Technique → information content entity. OBI_0000272 requires enough detail
# for independent process reproduction; a reusable technique category is less
# specific and is therefore not an OBI protocol (ADR 0014 review disposition).
# sstim:SensoryStimulationTechnique rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 .
#   Asserted in sstim-technique.ttl; commented here to avoid a duplicate.

# Protocol → OBI protocol. A preset is an information content entity that FOLLOWS
# a protocol via sstim:followsProtocol; it is not itself a protocol (see ADR 0014).
# sstim:SensoryStimulationProtocol rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000272 .
#   Asserted in sstim-technique.ttl; commented here to avoid a duplicate.

# Session instance → PROV Activity (stated in sstim-session.ttl; repeated here
# for cross-reference in alignment context)
# sstim:SessionInstance rdfs:subClassOf prov:Activity .

# Evidence claim → IAO information content entity.
# (Was iao:0000001 'conditional specification' — wrong; an evidence claim is
# not a conditional specification. iao:0000030 is the correct generalization.)
# sstim:EvidenceClaim rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 .
#   Asserted in sstim-evidence.ttl; commented here to avoid a duplicate.

# Frequency band → IAO information content entity
# sstim:FrequencyBand rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 .
#   Asserted in sstim-common.ttl, which reaches Core Plus; alignments is
#   Full-only, so asserting it here as well would add a duplicate triple
#   without widening the profile that carries the parent.

# Reference → IAO document
sstim:PublicSafeReference rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 .

# SSTIM controlled-value classes (including SensoryModality,
# StimulationMechanism, and IntendedEffect) are information categories, not
# the real-world roles, processes, or dispositions they classify (ADR 0021).

# ECO (Evidence & Conclusion Ontology) classifies evidence by TYPE / provenance,
# not by strength, so it has no clean match for the SSTIM evidence-tier concepts
# (speculative…established), which are GRADE-style strength grades. The former
# `sstim-v:tierEstablished skos:closeMatch eco:0006151` mapping was removed:
# ECO_0006151 is "documented statement evidence", not a systematic review, and
# ECO has no review/meta-analysis strength term. Left unmapped intentionally.


###########################################################################
# SNOMED CT alignments
###########################################################################

# Audited 2026-08-22. The identifier this file previously recorded, 229070002,
# denotes stretching exercises and not sensory stimulation; sensory stimulation
# is 226056003. Both were resolved by CodeSystem/$lookup on
# http://snomed.info/sct at tx.fhir.org, the HL7 FHIR terminology server, and
# the incorrect one is independently corroborated by the HL7 Europe hospital
# discharge encounter-type value set. browser.ihtsdotools.org, BioPortal and the
# Athena API all answer 403, and snomedbrowser.com is now a parked domain, so
# tx.fhir.org is the working instrument for any future SNOMED lookup.
#
# LICENCE, read before extending this section. SNOMED CT is licensed by SNOMED
# International. Brazil and Italy are both outside the 53 Member territories.
# These mappings assert IRIs under the public SNOMED CT URI Standard and
# deliberately carry no SNOMED description text, hierarchy, definition, or
# attribute content as data. Do not add SNOMED labels or child concepts here.
#
# An enquiry was sent to info@snomed.org on 2026-08-23 asking the narrow
# question: whether referencing concept identifiers as IRIs in an openly
# published mapping, without redistributing SNOMED CT content, requires an
# Affiliate Licence.
#
# SNOMED International replied on 2026-09-04, through its Chief Digital
# Information Officer: for this use, described as inclusion in some mapping
# statements, it would grant a no-fee "public good" Affiliate Licence, applied
# for through MLDS. The application was filed the same day in the name of
# Aeterni Anima and is awaiting approval, so the fee concern this comment used
# to carry is resolved.
#
# Two things the reply does not do, and both matter more than the fee.
#
# It did not rule on whether reference-only IRI use needs a licence at all. It
# offered one instead. Do not record it as having settled that question.
#
# And it does not change what may be published here. An Affiliate must issue
# sublicences to those using its products, and a sub-licensee may not distribute
# or share SNOMED CT Content or Derivatives; an anonymous CC BY 4.0 download can
# satisfy neither. So the rule above is unconditional and survives the licence:
# no SNOMED content in this file, whatever permission to "include more content"
# is granted. Withdrawing these mappings, if that ever becomes necessary, is
# still a one-commit change.
#
# Full record: docs/ontology/outreach/2026-09-04-snomed-affiliate-licence-reply.md
#
# Both relations follow the KR-09 extension/intension test, not label similarity.

sstim:SensoryStimulation skos:narrowMatch snomed:226056003 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim:SensoryStimulation ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:narrowMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget snomed:226056003 ;
    dct:date "2026-08-22"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Intension: the SNOMED concept carries an explicit therapeutic intent attribute, while this class admits experimental, expressive, accessibility and informational purposes and asserts no therapeutic commitment. Extension: the SNOMED concept subsumes clinical tactile technique, while this class covers binaural beats, photic driving and isochronic tones, which it does not subsume. Hence narrowMatch. Deliberately not closeMatch: asserting interchangeability would import a therapeutic framing this project disclaims (docs/concept/SCOPE.md and the no-medical-claims invariant)."@en .

sstim:Stimulation skos:relatedMatch snomed:122545008 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim:Stimulation ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:relatedMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget snomed:122545008 ;
    dct:date "2026-08-22"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The direction is left undetermined on purpose. This class's definition admits any deliberately parameterized process applied to an identified biological, sensory or neural process, under which the SNOMED concept would be narrower. Its scope note instead describes a neutral umbrella over sensory stimulation and interventional neuromodulation, under which the two merely overlap, because the SNOMED concept subsumes procedural stimulation that is neither. That is the same definition-versus-scope-note divergence recorded for sensory stimulation and non-neural recipients in docs/ontology/SENSORY_STIMULATION_SENSE_REVIEW.md. relatedMatch asserts the association without asserting a subsumption that a definition-authority decision could invalidate; upgrade to narrowMatch if the definition text is ruled normative."@en .

###########################################################################
# External upper-ontology term labels (display stubs)
#
# Local rdfs:label assertions for the external BFO/OBI/IAO IRIs referenced
# above and across the semantic dependency modules, so the knowledge browser
# renders readable
# names instead of opaque numeric IRIs. These are display aids, not
# authoritative definitions — the canonical labels live in BFO/OBI/IAO.
###########################################################################

bfo:0000015 rdfs:label "process"@en .
bfo:0000016 rdfs:label "disposition"@en .
obi:0000272 rdfs:label "protocol"@en .
cob:0000082 rdfs:label "planned process"@en .
iao:0000030 rdfs:label "information content entity"@en .



###########################################################################
# MeSH, UBERON and Wikidata alignments — tranche 1 (2026-09-05)
#
# Reviewed candidate set from docs/ontology/ALIGNMENT_CANDIDATES.md, which
# records the evidence per row: the authority's own scope note, the extension or
# intension divergence, and the candidates rejected and why. Read it before
# changing a predicate here.
#
# Every identifier was dereferenced at the service that mints it on 2026-09-05,
# and `make alignment-verify` re-runs that check: Wikidata for QIDs, the NLM
# endpoints for descriptors, EBI OLS4 for OBO IRIs. Label similarity generated
# the candidates and decided none of them, which is the rule this file has
# followed since the D012910 rejection.
#
# Three rules govern the predicates below.
#
# A therapy or indication framing on the external side, which several MeSH
# descriptors and Wikidata items carry and this vocabulary deliberately does
# not, is an intension difference, so those rows are closeMatch and not
# exactMatch.
#
# Where the external concept demonstrably contains or is contained by ours, the
# row says so with broadMatch or narrowMatch rather than flattening it to close.
#
# For neural systems and target sites, ADR 0021 holds a controlled value to be
# an information category rather than the entity it classifies. An anatomical
# class is that entity, so no row in that group is exactMatch, whatever the
# labels do.
#
# Not mapped, deliberately. sstim-v:targetCortex has no row: UBERON's "cortex"
# is the outer layer of any organ and subsumes adrenal cortex, while the
# intended sense here is probably cerebral cortex (UBERON:0000956, mesh
# D002540) and the definition, "cortical tissue as a stimulation target", does
# not exclude cerebellar cortex. That is a definition decision, not a mapping
# one. sstim-v:techUltrasoundNeuromod has none either: MeSH Ultrasonic Therapy
# and Wikidata's high-intensity focused ultrasound are both ablative, and low
# intensity focused ultrasound neuromodulation is a different technique wearing
# the same words.
###########################################################################

sstim-v:techTDCS skos:closeMatch mesh:D065908 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techTDCS ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D065908 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D065908> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The NLM descriptor is the same technique, constant low current through scalp electrodes, and differs only in framing it as therapy where this vocabulary asserts no therapeutic commitment. That framing difference is why closeMatch rather than exactMatch."@en .

sstim-v:techTDCS skos:closeMatch wd:Q603398 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techTDCS ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q603398 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q603398> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Same technique and the same therapy framing as the MeSH descriptor."@en .

sstim-v:techDBS skos:closeMatch mesh:D046690 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techDBS ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D046690 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D046690> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The descriptor is scoped by indication, naming therapy for movement disorders and Parkinson disease, while this concept carries no indication. The two are therefore not interchangeable; narrowMatch would be defensible if that scope note were read as normative rather than as indexing guidance."@en .

sstim-v:techDBS skos:closeMatch wd:Q618076 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techDBS ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q618076 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q618076> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Identical technique, described there as a surgical treatment. Treatment framing again, so close rather than exact."@en .

sstim-v:techElectroconvulsiveTherapy skos:closeMatch mesh:D004565 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techElectroconvulsiveTherapy ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D004565 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D004565> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The descriptor names the same procedure and adds its principal indications, severe affective disorders and schizophrenia, which this concept does not carry."@en .

sstim-v:techElectroconvulsiveTherapy skos:closeMatch wd:Q131543 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techElectroconvulsiveTherapy ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q131543 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q131543> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The item names the procedure with a thin intension, described only as a medical procedure, so closeMatch is the strongest defensible assertion."@en .

sstim-v:techVagusNerveStimulation skos:closeMatch mesh:D055536 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techVagusNerveStimulation ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D055536 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D055536> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The descriptor describes an implanted battery and adjunctive treatment of partial epilepsy and refractory depression. This concept covers implanted and transcutaneous delivery alike and names no indication, so it is the wider of the two."@en .

sstim-v:techVagusNerveStimulation skos:closeMatch wd:Q2062293 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techVagusNerveStimulation ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q2062293 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2062293> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Described as a medical treatment delivering electrical impulses to the vagus nerve. Same technique, treatment framing."@en .

sstim-v:techRepetitiveTMS skos:broadMatch mesh:D050781 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techRepetitiveTMS ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:broadMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D050781 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D050781> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The descriptor is transcranial magnetic stimulation generally, including the single-pulse probe used to assess cortical excitability. This concept is the repetitive protocol, and its own scope note holds that a single pulse used to measure is not neuromodulation, so the descriptor is strictly broader."@en .

sstim-v:techRepetitiveTMS skos:broadMatch wd:Q263962 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techRepetitiveTMS ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:broadMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q263962 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q263962> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The item is transcranial magnetic stimulation as a whole, which contains the repetitive protocol this concept names."@en .

sstim-v:techNeurofeedback skos:closeMatch mesh:D058765 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techNeurofeedback ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D058765 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D058765> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The descriptor is a technique to self-regulate brain activity presented as feedback, with no therapy framing and no restriction of the measured signal. This concept adds that the signal is typically EEG and that the feedback is rendered sensorily. The closest pair in this tranche; exactMatch is defensible and is not asserted only because the extension test has not been run in both directions."@en .

sstim-v:techNeurofeedback skos:closeMatch wd:Q1306920 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techNeurofeedback ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q1306920 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1306920> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Described as a type of biofeedback, which agrees with the placement here."@en .

sstim-v:techBiofeedback skos:closeMatch wd:Q864329 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techBiofeedback ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q864329 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q864329> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The item describes the general practice of instrumented awareness of a physiological function in order to influence it, which matches this concept closely."@en .

sstim-v:techBiofeedback skos:closeMatch mesh:D001676 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techBiofeedback ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D001676 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D001676> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The descriptor is Biofeedback, Psychology and is scoped both autonomically and therapeutically, naming conditions such as hypertension and migraine. This concept includes muscle tension and names no condition, so neither concept contains the other, which is what closeMatch is for."@en .

sstim-v:techPhoticDriving skos:broadMatch mesh:D010775 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techPhoticDriving ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:broadMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D010775 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D010775> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Photic Stimulation covers bright flashes and visual patterns used to elicit brain activity during electroencephalography. This concept is the periodic-flicker subset used to drive a rhythm at the flicker frequency, so the descriptor is broader."@en .

sstim-v:techASMR skos:relatedMatch wd:Q4826866 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techASMR ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:relatedMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q4826866 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q4826866> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The item is the response phenomenon. This concept is the stimulation technique intended to evoke it, which is the same technique-versus-phenomenon distinction already recorded for the binaural voice."@en .

sstim-v:techAcousticStartle skos:relatedMatch mesh:D013216 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:techAcousticStartle ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:relatedMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D013216 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D013216> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The descriptor is the startle reflex, that is the elicited response, not the eliciting protocol. A technique is related to the reflex it probes rather than close to it."@en .

sstim-v:phenomenonAuditorySteadyStateResponse skos:closeMatch wd:Q123224658 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:phenomenonAuditorySteadyStateResponse ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q123224658 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q123224658> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The item is the electrophysiological response to rapid auditory stimuli, which is what this concept names. closeMatch because the item draws no boundary against neighbouring evoked responses."@en .

sstim-v:phenomenonFrequencyFollowingResponse skos:narrowMatch wd:Q5502870 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:phenomenonFrequencyFollowingResponse ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:narrowMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q5502870 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5502870> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The item is explicitly auditory, an evoked potential generated by periodic or nearly-periodic auditory stimuli, while this concept is modality-neutral and covers any applied periodicity. The Wikidata concept is therefore the narrower of the two, and closeMatch would hide a real difference in extension."@en .

sstim-v:phenomenonAcousticStartleReflex skos:broadMatch mesh:D013216 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:phenomenonAcousticStartleReflex ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:broadMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D013216 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D013216> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Reflex, Startle is an involuntary response to any unexpected strong stimulus, with no modality restriction. This concept is the acoustic case, so the descriptor is broader."@en .

sstim-v:phenomenonSynapticTransmission skos:relatedMatch mesh:D009435 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:phenomenonSynapticTransmission ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:relatedMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D009435 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D009435> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-05"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The descriptor names the process itself. This concept names a change in that process, a phenomenon category in an evidence model, so the two are not the same kind of thing. Same reasoning as the multisensory-integration mapping above."@en .

